  "script_defect_found": {
    "summary": "check_archive() assumed digests.lock's image_id (docker inspect .Id at collection time) always equals the docker-save archive's manifest.json Config digest. Under Docker Desktop's containerd-backed image store (default since 4.34, active on this machine), .Id returns the pulled manifest(-list) digest instead.",
    "fix": "scripts/airgap/sbom.py check_archive() now also accepts a self-verified OCI index.json manifest digest (blob hash independently recomputed from archive bytes, never trusted from index.json's own claim) alongside the classic Config digest. digests.lock's format and install_from_airgap.sh (#5) were not touched.",
    "regression_tests_added": "scripts/airgap/test_sbom.sh: classic archive still requires Config digest; containerd-store archive accepts Config digest or self-verified index digest; unrelated digest rejected; forged index.json blob rejected; multi-manifest OCI index rejected",
